ame\": \"NXT LABS\", \"industry\": \"التكنولوجيا\", \"founded_year\": null, \"scale\": { \"employees\": null, \"offices\": \"مقرها في روالبندي، باكستان\", \"countries\": null }, \"expertise\": \"التوافر العالي، استعادة البيانات بعد الكوارث، وحلول السحابة\", \"main_products_services\": \"إدارة وتحسين قواعد البيانات، حلول استعادة البيانات بعد الكوارث، إدارة قواعد البيانات السحابية على AWS و Azure\", \"mission_statement\": null, \"core_values\": null, \"company_culture\": \"بيئة عمل ديناميكية مع فرص وفيرة للنمو المهني\", \"market_position\": \"شركة رائدة في مجال التكنولوجيا\" } } === END COMPANY BACKGROUND === TASK: Generate 2 open-ended questions to assess candidates for this role. REQUIREMENTS: - Difficulty Level: MEDIUM - Questions should require detailed, thoughtful responses - Include scenario-based and reflective questions - Provide keywords/criteria for AI scoring - Include sample strong responses Return ONLY valid JSON with NO markdown, NO explanations: { \"questions\": [ { \"question_en\": \"English question text\", \"question_ar\": \"نص السؤال بالعربية\", \"expected_keywords\": [\"keyword1\", \"keyword2\", \"keyword3\"], \"scoring_criteria_en\": \"What to look for in a good answer\", \"scoring_criteria_ar\": \"ما يجب البحث عنه في الإجابة الجيدة\", \"sample_strong_response_en\": \"Example of a strong answer\", \"sample_strong_response_ar\": \"مثال على إجابة قوية\", \"min_word_count\": 100, \"max_word_count\": 500, \"difficulty\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"behavioral/analytical/creative\" } ] }"}
{"provider":"openai","timestamp":1766749508725,"prompt":"You are a STRICT and CRITICAL Technical Recruiter evaluating case study submissions. CRITICAL EVALUATION STANDARDS: - ONE-LINERS: Maximum 30/100 - VAGUE ANSWERS: Maximum 50/100 - MISSING PRIORITIZATION: -20 minimum - NO METRICS: -15 points - NO IMPLEMENTATION: -15 points SCORING RUBRIC: - 90-100: Exceptional - Detailed, strategic, prioritized, with metrics and implementation - 75-89: Good - Comprehensive with most elements - 60-74: Acceptable - Main points but lacks depth - 40-59: Poor - Superficial, missing elements - 0-39: Unacceptable - One-liners or irrelevant ⚠️ AI DETECTION RESULTS: ⚠️ ALERT: 1 out of 1 answers flagged as AI-generated (73.2% average confidence) Detailed AI Detection per Question: Q1: 73.2% AI probability (Copyleaks) IMPORTANT: When providing feedback, YOU MUST mention AI detection if confidence is above 60%. For questions with high AI probability (>70%), your feedback MUST include: - \"⚠️ This answer shows high probability of AI-generated content (XX%)\" TECHNICAL SKILLS TO EVALUATE (8 total): 1. PostgreSQL (Category: Database, Required: Yes) 2. AWS (Category: Cloud, Required: Yes) 3. Collaboration (Category: Soft Skill, Required: Yes) 4. Data Security (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 5. MySQL (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 6. Disaster Recovery (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 7. Azure (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 8. Performance Tuning (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) For EACH skill, provide: - A score from 0-10 based on evidence in answers - Specific evidence/quotes from the candidate's responses - Assessment of proficiency level CUSTOM ASSESSMENT QUESTIONS TO EVALUATE (2 total): CQ1 [Open-Ended] [Weight: 1.00x] (ID: 76): Question: Describe a time when you had to design a disaster recovery solution for a complex database system. What challenges did you face and how did you overcome them? Max Score: 100 Answer: When designing a disaster recovery solution for a complex database system, I faced challenges such as ensuring minimal downtime, data consistency, and cost management. One key issue was setting up automated backups and replication to prevent data loss during failures. To overcome this, I implemented point-in-time backups and multi-region replication to ensure high availability. I also configured failover mechanisms to automatically switch to a secondary database in case of primary database failure. Testing the solution regularly was crucial to ensure it worked as expected, and I balanced cost by choosing the appropriate recovery point objectives (RPO) and recovery time objectives (RTO) based on business needs. CQ2 [Open-Ended] [Weight: 1.00x] (ID: 77): Question: Reflect on a situation where you collaborated with a development team to optimize a cloud database solution. What strategies did you implement and what was the outcome? Max Score: 100 Answer: collaborated with a development team to optimize a cloud database solution by focusing on performance, scalability, and cost-efficiency. Key strategies included: Database Indexing: Worked with the team to identify and create indexes on frequently queried columns to speed up search times. Query Optimization: Analyzed slow queries and helped refactor them to minimize resource usage. Auto-scaling: Configured auto-scaling for the cloud database to adjust resources based on demand. Data Archiving: Implemented archiving for older, less-accessed data to improve query performance. The outcome was a more efficient, faster database with reduced costs due to optimized resource usage and improved response times for end users. CUSTOM QUESTION SCORING INSTRUCTIONS: - Questions with higher weights are MORE IMPORTANT and should be evaluated more thoroughly - For coding/SQL questions: Evaluate correctness, efficiency, best practices, edge cases - For open-ended/writing: Evaluate clarity, depth, relevance, structure - For video responses: Return score as null and feedback \"Pending manual review - recruiter must watch and score the video submission\". Video responses CANNOT be auto-scored. - For Excel tasks: Evaluate formula correctness, data analysis approach - For situational judgment: Evaluate decision-making, reasoning, practical application - Score each on 0-100 scale with detailed feedback (except video which should be null) CRITICAL: ALL TEXT FEEDBACK MUST BE IN English. JOB/ASSESSMENT: Senior Database Engineer: HA/DR & Cloud Solutions CANDIDATE: Muhammad Muneeb CASE STUDY QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS: Q1: Identify specific database configurations that could be optimized to reduce current latency issues. What steps would you take to implement these optimizations? [⚠️ AI Detection: 73.2%] A: To optimize database configurations and reduce latency issues, focus on these areas: Indexing: Add or optimize indexes for frequently queried columns to speed up data retrieval. Query Optimization: Refactor slow queries, ensuring they are efficient and avoid unnecessary joins or subqueries. Connection Pooling: Use connection pooling to reduce the overhead of creating and destroying database connections. Caching: Implement query caching for frequently accessed data to reduce database load. Data Partitioning/Sharding: Split large datasets into smaller, more manageable parts to improve read/write performance. Database Configuration Tuning: Adjust parameters like buffer_size, cache_size, and work_mem based on the database workload. Steps to implement: Review and analyze current database performance (e.g., using slow query logs or monitoring tools). Apply index optimizations based on query analysis. Refactor and optimize slow queries. Implement connection pooling and caching mechanisms. Tune database parameters according to performance benchmarks. Monitor results to ensure improvements. Q2: How would you design a disaster recovery strategy to minimize downtime during a system outage? Include specific technologies you would use. A: NO ANSWER Q3: Consider the current deployment frequency and incident response time. What process improvements could be implemented to enhance these metrics? A: NO ANSWER Q4: Discuss how you would collaborate with the development team to ensure database requirements are met during sprints. What challenges might you face? A: NO ANSWER Q5: What tools or frameworks would you use to monitor database performance and proactively address potential issues? A: NO ANSWER Q6: Given the existing cloud infrastructure, how would you approach scaling the databases on AWS and Azure to handle increased throughput? A: NO ANSWER Q7: Evaluate the current test coverage percentage for database changes. How would you improve this to ensure code quality and system reliability? A: NO ANSWER NOTE: Questions with higher weights are MORE IMPORTANT and should be evaluated more thoroughly. RETURN ONLY VALID JSON (no markdown, no explanations): { \"overall_score\": <0-100>, \"rating\": \"<Poor|Fair|Good|Excellent>\", \"ai_detected\": true, \"recruiter_feedback\": \"<Comprehensive feedback in English>\", \"question_scores\": [{ \"question_number\": 1, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English - mention AI detection>\" },{ \"question_number\": 2, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\" },{ \"question_number\": 3, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\" },{ \"question_number\": 4, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\" },{ \"question_number\": 5, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\" },{ \"question_number\": 6, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\" },{ \"question_number\": 7, \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\" }], \"skill_scores\": [{ \"skill_name\": \"PostgreSQL\", \"category\": \"Database\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"AWS\", \"category\": \"Cloud\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"Collaboration\", \"category\": \"Soft Skill\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"Data Security\", \"category\": \"Technical\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"MySQL\", \"category\": \"Technical\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"Disaster Recovery\", \"category\": \"Technical\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"Azure\", \"category\": \"Technical\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true },{ \"skill_name\": \"Performance Tuning\", \"category\": \"Technical\", \"score\": <0-10>, \"evidence\": \"<Specific evidence from answers in English>\", \"is_required\": true }], \"psychometric_scores\": [], \"custom_question_scores\": [{ \"question_id\": 76, \"question_type\": \"open_ended\", \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\", \"code_quality\": null },{ \"question_id\": 77, \"question_type\": \"open_ended\", \"score\": <0-100>, \"feedback\": \"<Detailed feedback in English>\", \"code_quality\": null }], \"final_recommendation\": \"<Hire|Interview|Review|Reject>\" }"}
