{"provider":"openai","timestamp":1767179900713,"prompt":"You are an expert at creating professional coding challenges for software developer candidates. IMPORTANT: If ADDITIONAL CONTEXT includes a CASE STUDY DESCRIPTION and TABLE SUMMARIES, incorporate scenario data where appropriate (e.g., sample inputs derived from table values or data summaries) and reference specific metrics or named entities. JOB CONTEXT: Job Title: Full Stack Developer Description: We are seeking a passionate Full Stack Developer to join our dynamic development team in Islamabad, Pakistan. This role is perfect for a mid-level professional with 3-5 years of experience who is eager to apply their technical skills to challenging projects and contribute to innovative solutions. As a Full Stack Developer, you will be responsible for designing and implementing both client-side and server-side applications. You will work closely with our team to ensure seamless integration and optimal performance of our software solutions. Your role will be crucial in delivering high-quality applications that meet user needs and business goals. Key Responsibilities: • Develop and maintain web applications using modern frameworks and technologies • Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features • Ensure the performance, quality, and responsiveness of applications • Identify and correct bottlenecks and fix bugs • Participate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback • Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability • Implement security and data protection practices • Stay updated with emerging technologies and industry trends ADDITIONAL CONTEXT: CONTEXT USAGE INSTRUCTION: Use the CASE STUDY DESCRIPTION and TABLE SUMMARIES below as the primary source when generating module questions; reference specific metrics, table titles, and named entities when relevant. CASE STUDY DESCRIPTION: The company is a software development firm specializing in creating both client-side and server-side applications. With offices located in Islamabad, Pakistan, the company has a dynamic development team that focuses on delivering high-quality software solutions. Currently, the company is dealing with an operational challenge involving performance bottlenecks and security vulnerabilities in their web applications. The applications, built using modern frameworks, are facing issues due to increasing technical debt, impacting deployment frequency and system availability. The objective is to optimize the applications for better speed and scalability, while implementing improved security measures to protect data. These challenges have led to a decline in the velocity points and an increase in incident response time, affecting overall productivity and customer satisfaction. TABLE SUMMARIES: - Current Metrics & Performance: columns: Metric | Current Value | Target | Variance | Trend. sample_rows: {\"metric_name\":\"Deployment Frequency\",\"current_value\":\"5 times/month\",\"target_value\":\"10 times/month\",\"variance\":\"-50%\",\"trend\":\"↓ Declining\"} ; {\"metric_name\":\"System Availability\",\"current_value\":\"85%\",\"target_value\":\"99%\",\"variance\":\"-14%\",\"trend\":\"↓ Declining\"} ; {\"metric_name\":\"Incident Response Time\",\"current_value\":\"2 hours\",\"target_value\":\"30 minutes\",\"variance\":\"+300%\",\"trend\":\"↓ Declining\"} - Situation/Context Data: columns: Item | Status | Impact Level | Details. sample_rows: {\"item\":\"Performance Bottleneck\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"impact\":\"High\",\"notes\":\"Causing delays in deployment\"} ; {\"item\":\"Security Vulnerability\",\"status\":\"Pending\",\"impact\":\"Critical\",\"notes\":\"Potential threat to data integrity\"} - Available Resources & Constraints: columns: Resource Type | Availability | Cost/Effort | Constraint. sample_rows: {\"resource_type\":\"Development Team\",\"availability\":\"Fully available\",\"cost_or_effort\":\"Included\",\"constraint\":\"Time-bound\"} ; {\"resource_type\":\"Budget for Tools\",\"availability\":\"Limited\",\"cost_or_effort\":\"Additional budget needed\",\"constraint\":\"Capacity limited\"} FALLBACK CONTEXT: === COMPANY BACKGROUND === { \"en\": { \"company\": { \"name\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"industry\": \"Software Development\", \"founded\": \"Not Mentioned\" }, \"scale\": { \"employees\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"offices\": \"Islamabad, Pakistan\", \"countries\": \"Not Mentioned\" }, \"expertise\": { \"specializations\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"products_services\": \"Client-side and server-side applications\" }, \"mission\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"core_values\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"culture\": \"Dynamic development team\", \"market_position\": \"Not Mentioned\" }, \"ar\": { \"company\": { \"name\": \"غير مذكور\", \"industry\": \"تطوير البرمجيات\", \"founded\": \"غير مذكور\" }, \"scale\": { \"employees\": \"غير مذكور\", \"offices\": \"إسلام آباد، باكستان\", \"countries\": \"غير مذكور\" }, \"expertise\": { \"specializations\": \"غير مذكور\", \"products_services\": \"تطبيقات الواجهة الأمامية والخلفية\" }, \"mission\": \"غير مذكور\", \"core_values\": \"غير مذكور\", \"culture\": \"فريق تطوير ديناميكي\", \"market_position\": \"غير مذكور\" } } === END COMPANY BACKGROUND === TASK: Generate 1 coding challenges to assess candidates for this role. REQUIREMENTS: - Difficulty Level: MEDIUM - Include clear problem statement - Provide input/output examples - Include test cases for validation - Support multiple programming languages (Python, JavaScript, Java) Return ONLY valid JSON with NO markdown, NO explanations: { \"challenges\": [ { \"title_en\": \"Challenge Title\", \"title_ar\": \"عنوان التحدي\", \"problem_statement_en\": \"Detailed problem description\", \"problem_statement_ar\": \"وصف المشكلة بالتفصيل\", \"input_format_en\": \"Description of input format\", \"input_format_ar\": \"وصف تنسيق الإدخال\", \"output_format_en\": \"Description of expected output\", \"output_format_ar\": \"وصف المخرجات المتوقعة\", \"constraints_en\": [\"Time constraint\", \"Memory constraint\"], \"constraints_ar\": [\"قيد الوقت\", \"قيد الذاكرة\"], \"examples\": [ { \"input\": \"sample input\", \"output\": \"expected output\", \"explanation_en\": \"Why this output\", \"explanation_ar\": \"لماذا هذا الإخراج\" } ], \"test_cases\": [ { \"input\": \"test1\", \"expected_output\": \"output1\", \"is_hidden\": false }, { \"input\": \"test2\", \"expected_output\": \"output2\", \"is_hidden\": true } ], \"starter_code\": { \"python\": \"def solution(input):\\n # Your code here\\n pass\", \"javascript\": \"function solution(input) {\\n // Your code here\\n}\", \"java\": \"public class Solution {\\n public static String solution(String input) {\\n // Your code here\\n return \\\"\\\";\\n }\\n}\" }, \"difficulty\": \"medium\", \"tags\": [\"arrays\", \"strings\", \"algorithms\"] } ] }"}
{"provider":"openai","timestamp":1767179907384,"prompt":"You are an expert at creating professional writing assessment exercises for candidates. JOB CONTEXT: Job Title: Full Stack Developer Description: We are seeking a passionate Full Stack Developer to join our dynamic development team in Islamabad, Pakistan. This role is perfect for a mid-level professional with 3-5 years of experience who is eager to apply their technical skills to challenging projects and contribute to innovative solutions. As a Full Stack Developer, you will be responsible for designing and implementing both client-side and server-side applications. You will work closely with our team to ensure seamless integration and optimal performance of our software solutions. Your role will be crucial in delivering high-quality applications that meet user needs and business goals. Key Responsibilities: • Develop and maintain web applications using modern frameworks and technologies • Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features • Ensure the performance, quality, and responsiveness of applications • Identify and correct bottlenecks and fix bugs • Participate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback • Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability • Implement security and data protection practices • Stay updated with emerging technologies and industry trends ADDITIONAL CONTEXT: CONTEXT USAGE INSTRUCTION: Use the CASE STUDY DESCRIPTION and TABLE SUMMARIES below as the primary source when generating module questions; reference specific metrics, table titles, and named entities when relevant. CASE STUDY DESCRIPTION: The company is a software development firm specializing in creating both client-side and server-side applications. With offices located in Islamabad, Pakistan, the company has a dynamic development team that focuses on delivering high-quality software solutions. Currently, the company is dealing with an operational challenge involving performance bottlenecks and security vulnerabilities in their web applications. The applications, built using modern frameworks, are facing issues due to increasing technical debt, impacting deployment frequency and system availability. The objective is to optimize the applications for better speed and scalability, while implementing improved security measures to protect data. These challenges have led to a decline in the velocity points and an increase in incident response time, affecting overall productivity and customer satisfaction. TABLE SUMMARIES: - Current Metrics & Performance: columns: Metric | Current Value | Target | Variance | Trend. sample_rows: {\"metric_name\":\"Deployment Frequency\",\"current_value\":\"5 times/month\",\"target_value\":\"10 times/month\",\"variance\":\"-50%\",\"trend\":\"↓ Declining\"} ; {\"metric_name\":\"System Availability\",\"current_value\":\"85%\",\"target_value\":\"99%\",\"variance\":\"-14%\",\"trend\":\"↓ Declining\"} ; {\"metric_name\":\"Incident Response Time\",\"current_value\":\"2 hours\",\"target_value\":\"30 minutes\",\"variance\":\"+300%\",\"trend\":\"↓ Declining\"} - Situation/Context Data: columns: Item | Status | Impact Level | Details. sample_rows: {\"item\":\"Performance Bottleneck\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"impact\":\"High\",\"notes\":\"Causing delays in deployment\"} ; {\"item\":\"Security Vulnerability\",\"status\":\"Pending\",\"impact\":\"Critical\",\"notes\":\"Potential threat to data integrity\"} - Available Resources & Constraints: columns: Resource Type | Availability | Cost/Effort | Constraint. sample_rows: {\"resource_type\":\"Development Team\",\"availability\":\"Fully available\",\"cost_or_effort\":\"Included\",\"constraint\":\"Time-bound\"} ; {\"resource_type\":\"Budget for Tools\",\"availability\":\"Limited\",\"cost_or_effort\":\"Additional budget needed\",\"constraint\":\"Capacity limited\"} FALLBACK CONTEXT: === COMPANY BACKGROUND === { \"en\": { \"company\": { \"name\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"industry\": \"Software Development\", \"founded\": \"Not Mentioned\" }, \"scale\": { \"employees\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"offices\": \"Islamabad, Pakistan\", \"countries\": \"Not Mentioned\" }, \"expertise\": { \"specializations\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"products_services\": \"Client-side and server-side applications\" }, \"mission\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"core_values\": \"Not Mentioned\", \"culture\": \"Dynamic development team\", \"market_position\": \"Not Mentioned\" }, \"ar\": { \"company\": { \"name\": \"غير مذكور\", \"industry\": \"تطوير البرمجيات\", \"founded\": \"غير مذكور\" }, \"scale\": { \"employees\": \"غير مذكور\", \"offices\": \"إسلام آباد، باكستان\", \"countries\": \"غير مذكور\" }, \"expertise\": { \"specializations\": \"غير مذكور\", \"products_services\": \"تطبيقات الواجهة الأمامية والخلفية\" }, \"mission\": \"غير مذكور\", \"core_values\": \"غير مذكور\", \"culture\": \"فريق تطوير ديناميكي\", \"market_position\": \"غير مذكور\" } } === END COMPANY BACKGROUND === TASK: Generate 1 writing exercises to assess candidates for this role. REQUIREMENTS: - Difficulty Level: MEDIUM - Include professional writing scenarios (emails, reports, proposals) - Provide clear context and requirements - Include evaluation rubric Return ONLY valid JSON with NO markdown, NO explanations: { \"exercises\": [ { \"title_en\": \"Exercise Title\", \"title_ar\": \"عنوان التمرين\", \"type\": \"email/report/proposal/memo\", \"scenario_en\": \"Detailed scenario and context\", \"scenario_ar\": \"السيناريو والسياق بالتفصيل\", \"requirements_en\": [\"Must include X\", \"Should address Y\", \"Format as Z\"], \"requirements_ar\": [\"يجب أن يتضمن X\", \"يجب معالجة Y\", \"التنسيق كـ Z\"], \"audience_en\": \"Who will read this\", \"audience_ar\": \"من سيقرأ هذا\", \"word_count_min\": 200, \"word_count_max\": 500, \"rubric\": { \"clarity\": { \"weight\": 25, \"description_en\": \"Clear and coherent\", \"description_ar\": \"واضح ومتماسك\" }, \"grammar\": { \"weight\": 20, \"description_en\": \"Proper grammar and spelling\", \"description_ar\": \"قواعد وإملاء صحيحة\" }, \"structure\": { \"weight\": 20, \"description_en\": \"Well-organized\", \"description_ar\": \"منظم جيداً\" }, \"relevance\": { \"weight\": 20, \"description_en\": \"Addresses the topic\", \"description_ar\": \"يعالج الموضوع\" }, \"professionalism\": { \"weight\": 15, \"description_en\": \"Professional tone\", \"description_ar\": \"نبرة مهنية\" } }, \"difficulty\": \"medium\" } ] }"}
{"provider":"openai","timestamp":1767180097795,"prompt":"You are a STRICT and CRITICAL Technical Recruiter evaluating case study submissions. CRITICAL EVALUATION STANDARDS: - ONE-LINERS: Maximum 30/100 - VAGUE ANSWERS: Maximum 50/100 - MISSING PRIORITIZATION: -20 minimum - NO METRICS: -15 points - NO IMPLEMENTATION: -15 points SCORING RUBRIC: - 90-100: Exceptional - Detailed, strategic, prioritized, with metrics and implementation - 75-89: Good - Comprehensive with most elements - 60-74: Acceptable - Main points but lacks depth - 40-59: Poor - Superficial, missing elements - 0-39: Unacceptable - One-liners or irrelevant ⚠️ AI DETECTION RESULTS: ⚠️ ALERT: 2 out of 2 answers flagged as AI-generated (73.2% average confidence) Detailed AI Detection per Question: CQ141: 73.2% AI probability (Copyleaks) CQ142: 73.2% AI probability (Copyleaks) IMPORTANT: When providing feedback, YOU MUST mention AI detection if confidence is above 60%. For questions with high AI probability (>70%), your feedback MUST include: - \"⚠️ This answer shows high probability of AI-generated content (XX%)\" TECHNICAL SKILLS TO EVALUATE (8 total): 1. JavaScript (Category: Programming, Required: Yes) 2. Collaboration (Category: Soft Skill, Required: Yes) 3. Communication (Category: Soft Skill, Required: Yes) 4. Problem Solving (Category: Soft Skill, Required: Yes) 5. Code Review (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 6. Full Stack Development (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 7. Modern Frameworks (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) 8. Security and Data Protection (Category: Technical, Required: Yes) For EACH skill, provide: - A score from 0-10 based on evidence in answers - Specific evidence/quotes from the candidate's responses - Assessment of proficiency level CUSTOM ASSESSMENT QUESTIONS TO EVALUATE (2 total): CQ1 [Code Challenge] [Weight: 50.00x] (ID: 141): Question: You are part of a team responsible for optimizing the deployment frequency of a software application. Currently, the deployment frequency is 5 times per month, but the target is 10 times per month. Write a function that analyzes an array of deployment dates and calculates the current deployment frequency. The function should then determine the necessary changes required to meet the target frequency. Max Score: 100 Answer: from datetime import datetime from collections import Counter def calculate_deployment_frequency(deployment_dates, target_frequency=10): # Convert date strings into datetime objects deployment_dates = [datetime.strptime(date, '%Y-%m-%d') for date in deployment_dates] # Extract the year and month for each deployment months = [date.strftime('%Y-%m') for date in deployment_dates] # Count how many deployments per month month_counts = Counter(months) # Calculate current deployment frequency (average per month) total_deployments = sum(month_counts.values()) months_with_deployments = len(month_counts) current_frequency = total_deployments / months_with_deployments if months_with_deployments else 0 # Determine the changes needed to reach the target frequency required_deployments = target_frequency * months_with_deployments additional_deployments_needed = required_deployments - total_deployments return { 'current_frequency': current_frequency, 'total_deployments': total_deployments, 'required_deployments': required_deployments, 'additional_deployments_needed': additional_deployments_needed } # Example usage: deployment_dates = [ '2025-12-01', '2025-12-03', '2025-12-10', '2025-12-15', '2025-12-20', '2025-11-05', '2025-11-12', '2025-11-20', '2025-11-28', '2025-10-01' ] result = calculate_deployment_frequency(deployment_dates) print(result) [⚠️ AI Detection: 73.2%] CQ2 [Writing Exercise] [Weight: 50.00x] (ID: 142): Question: As a Full Stack Developer at our company, you have identified that the deployment frequency of our web applications is significantly below the target. You need to draft a proposal outlining your strategies to improve deployment frequency from 5 times/month to the target of 10 times/month. Consider the current challenges such as performance bottlenecks, security vulnerabilities, and technical debt. Provide a detailed plan including proposed methodologies, the role of the development team, and any additional resources required. Max Score: 100 Answer: ### Proposal: Improving Deployment Frequency from 5 to 10 Deployments Per Month **Objective:** The goal of this proposal is to outline strategies and actions that will enable the team to double our deployment frequency, from 5 deployments per month to 10. By improving deployment frequency, we can deliver new features and bug fixes more rapidly, ultimately improving our product's agility and customer satisfaction. ### **Key Challenges:** 1. **Performance Bottlenecks:** * Slow build and test processes can delay deployments and create a bottleneck. * Long deployment times (especially in staging or production environments) affect the ability to deploy frequently. 2. **Security Vulnerabilities:** * Regular deployments must ensure that security patches are applied immediately, which requires a smooth and secure CI/CD pipeline. * Inconsistent or infrequent deployment frequency can lead to outdated versions of the application in production, increasing security risks. 3. **Technical Debt:** * Unresolved technical debt can slow down development cycles and deployment preparation, leading to longer release cycles. * Legacy code or poorly maintained systems can cause unpredictable behavior, making deployments more complex and error-prone. ### **Strategies to Improve Deployment Frequency:** #### 1. **Enhance the CI/CD Pipeline** * **Goal:** Automate the process of testing, building, and deploying to ensure fast and reliable deployments. * **Action Plan:** * **Automate Testing:** Implement a comprehensive suite of automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests. This ensures that we catch bugs earlier in the development cycle. * **Parallelize Builds and Tests:** Use parallelization techniques in CI/CD pipelines to run multiple tests and builds concurrently, speeding up the process. * **Incremental Builds:** Implement incremental builds to ensure only modified code is compiled and tested, reducing unnecessary build times. * **Continuous Deployment:** Move towards a continuous deployment approach where every successful commit to the repository is automatically deployed to staging and, in some cases, production. This reduces the friction of manual deployments and ensures that small updates can be deployed more frequently. #### 2. **Address Performance Bottlenecks** * **Goal:** Reduce deployment time and improve the performance of build and deployment pipelines. * **Action Plan:** * **Optimize Build Scripts:** Review and optimize existing build scripts to remove unnecessary steps and reduce build time. * **Optimize Database Migrations:** Implement safer, faster database migrations to prevent long downtimes during deployments. Consider using tools like **Liquibase** or **Flyway** for version-controlled database schemas. * **Use Blue-Green or Canary Deployments:** Reduce downtime by implementing **Blue-Green** or **Canary Deployments**. These strategies allow for smoother transitions between application versions, reducing the impact on users and increasing deployment frequency. * **Containerization:** If not already done, use containerization (e.g., Docker) to make deployments faster and more consistent across environments. * **Monitor Performance:** Set up monitoring for build and deployment times to identify and fix performance bottlenecks continuously. #### 3. **Address Security Vulnerabilities** * **Goal:** Ensure security patches are deployed quickly and vulnerabilities are caught earlier in the process. * **Action Plan:** * **Automated Security Testing:** Integrate security testing tools into the CI/CD pipeline (e.g., **Snyk**, **Dependabot** for dependency checks, **OWASP ZAP** for web application security testing). * **Frequent Patch Releases:** Ensure that our pipeline can quickly apply patches and updates, particularly for security vulnerabilities. Implement a **\"patch-and-deploy\"** workflow where security fixes can be deployed with minimal manual intervention. * **Role-Based Access Controls (RBAC):** Ensure that only the necessary team members have deployment access and are following a least-privilege model to prevent accidental or unauthorized changes. #### 4. **Tackle Technical Debt** * **Goal:** Ensure codebase quality and maintainability to reduce bottlenecks caused by technical debt. * **Action Plan:** * **Refactor Legacy Code:** Prioritize critical areas of legacy code that are slowing down deployments. Plan regular refactoring sprints to eliminate areas of high technical debt. * **Use Code Reviews and Linting:** Enforce strict code review policies and introduce static analysis tools (e.g., **SonarQube**, **ESLint**) to catch issues early in the development cycle. * **Modularize the Codebase:** Break down monolithic applications into smaller microservices or modular components. This enables smaller, more frequent updates, and reduces the risk of deployment failures. #### 5. **Development Team Collaboration & Communication** * **Goal:** Foster a culture of collaboration to improve efficiency in the deployment process. * **Action Plan:** * **Cross-Functional Teams:** Create cross-functional teams that include members from development, operations, security, and QA to work together on improving the deployment pipeline. * **Daily Standups/Weekly Check-ins:** Use agile practices such as daily standups and weekly retrospectives to identify and address roadblocks in the deployment process. * **Ownership of Deployments:** Empower individual team members to take ownership of specific components or features that can be deployed independently. This allows for smaller, more manageable deployments. * **Clear Documentation:** Ensure that the deployment process is well-documented, including how to handle rollbacks, emergency fixes, and deployment best practices. #### 6. **Tools an"}
